,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4.256999284,"data":"  In July 2020, 52% of U.S. 18- to 29-year-olds lived with a\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4.257005253,"data":"  parent (26.6 million) -- the first majority since the Great Depression era,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4.25701066,"data":"  exceeding even the 1940 record of 48% and the Feb 2020 pre-pandemic share of\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4.257015738,"data":"  47%. With n = 51.2 million, both nulls are rejected overwhelmingly\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":4.257021285,"data":"  (p \u003c 1e-15). Young men exceed young women (55% vs 49%) and the youngest\n"}
